# index.html had MIXED line endings - mostly CRLF, with LF-only regions and, at one
# point, lone CR characters used as line separators. That mix cost real time: a lone CR
# is a line terminator to a JavaScript engine but not to sed or git, so live code
# displayed as commented out, and removing the lone CRs let core.autocrlf normalize the
# whole file, turning a six-character fix into a 2743-line diff.
#
# The file is now uniformly CRLF and is pinned that way, so diffs stay legible and an
# editor cannot quietly reintroduce the mix.
*.html text eol=crlf
*.js text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
